  "query_preview": "..\nToday: Cold airmass across the region is shallowing out this \nmorning. A low stratus deck sits just over this inversion. Some \nclearing this morning will allow temps to cool further under open \nskies and could allow some to dip into the single digits. Winds \nwill increase a bit today from the E-SE as surface high pressure \ndrops SE into the Dakotas.\n\nTonight through Thursday, A slow warm up and mainly dry \nconditions are expected into Thursday as a ridge slowly approaches\nfrom the west. Highs by Thursday should be in the mid 40s as a \nridge crests and exits the region, there should also be near \novercast high- cirrus clouds due to the chinook arch. \n\nFriday: A cold front will arrive around mid-day plus or minus 6\nhours. This will control whether the last day of the ridge exit \nis the warmest or not. Behind this front will be strong NW winds \nwhich could easily lead to a Lake Wind Advisory. Increased chance\nfor precipitation just behind the front also exist with isolated \nto scattered light rain or snow showers possible. \n\nFriday night onward: Ensembles have started to move into the\nconsensus of a northwest to zonal flow pattern, but still have\nvariations of sub-synoptic ridges and troughs. Near to above\nnormal temps are expected with isolated chances(10-30%) for light\nshowers possible. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & NBM DEVIATIONS:\nMajor deviations from NBM were made into the first 12 to 18 hours\nof the hourly forecast for hourly Sky and CloudBase grids. Most \nmajor models are showing SKC skies for about the last 18 hours \nwhile near OVC skies around 1000-3000 foot were clearly apparent \non almost all SFC ceilometers as well as satellite data across \neastern MT and western ND. This is a massive mis-calculation by \nthe models that could dangerously impact the aviation community \nand TAFs and had to be corrected for in the NDFD. \n\n- Moderate to High confidence(50-80%) through Thursday. \n\n- Moderate confidence(40-60%) Friday through the end of forecast. \n\nTFJ/GAH",
